-## branch_pr mode
-
-**Where work happens:** in a per-task branch/worktree.
-
-**Who closes the task:** INTEGRATOR on the base branch after merge.
-
-**Key outputs:**
+Use them when a human/operator is investigating drift or when Agentplane explicitly returns a
+manual recovery boundary. Low-level task, worktree, PR, verification, integration, release, and
+cleanup commands remain available through `agentplane help --all`; they are not the agent happy
+path.
 
-- PR artifacts are required under `.agentplane/tasks/<task-id>/pr/`.
-- Canonical task writes happen on the base branch only.
-- Handoff notes are appended during review and carried into closure.
-- Hosted PRs and server-side required checks are separate from local `agentplane pr ...` artifacts.
+Never execute a raw route string as shell. Use typed action fields and exact argv returned by the
+CLI.
 
